n for child psychiatric disorders in a community sample</article-title><source>British Journal of Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>534</fpage><lpage>539</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11102329</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1192/bjp.177.6.534</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Skovgaard</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Houmann</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Landorph</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Christiansen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment and classification of psychopathology in epidemiological research of children 0&#x02013;3 years of age. A review of the literature</article-title><source>Eur child Adolesc Psychiatry</source><year>2004</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>337</fpage><lpage>346</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15619045</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00787-004-0393-z</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>